[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-3.801,-1.536);
\coordinate (C) at (1.013,-2.506);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {$91$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$109$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,right] {$60$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(A)!0.32cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(A)!0.32cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(A)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.75] {angle=C--B--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The right angle is at the top vertex. Evaluate $\cos\theta$ as a decimal correct to $4$ decimal places.
